Item 13 (Workspace, bridge, group and rule graphics) is done and the gate passes: 1438 Racket tests plus the Chez checks, in about 6 minutes. `chez_scheme/original/` and `tests/golden/` are untouched. I've marked the item `[x]`, written PROGRESS.md (now 14/18 solved) and left everything uncommitted for the driver.

**Watching changes nothing.** All 109 golden runs give byte-identical traces with the Workspace window attached and drawing. The run where the original crashes also crashes at the same point, with the same trace up to the crash. I checked that the test would notice a change: making one graphics procedure draw a single random number breaks 119 checks.

**How it's split:**
- **Engine side:** the code the model calls directly when workspace graphics are on, which only builds drawing expressions, moved into the engine verbatim. That is general-graphics.ss's shape builders plus group-, bridge- and rule-graphics.ss. The engine still doesn't load racket/draw.
- **View side:** the windows, fonts and colours are in `racket/gui/views.rkt`, which uses racket/draw but not racket/gui. Its `define` and `set!` pass any name the engine owns to the engine's `set-global!`, so the ported files stay verbatim.
- **Windows:** windows are offscreen for now; item 15 can swap in real ones.

**Pictures.** I rendered six moments of golden runs to PNG and looked at each. `abc abd mrrjjj` at 513 codelets matches the dissertation's figure taken at the same moment. The others are an answer, a snag shown as a Trace event, run7's `wyz` answer and its Memory description, and a justify run; they match the dissertation's style. All six are now pixel-snapshot tests.

**Problems found on the way, all fixed:**
- **`record-case`:** compat's version raised an error on extra arguments; Chez ignores them. trace.ss relies on that, so every run with graphics on crashed at its first answer.
- **Text erasing:** the graphics erase text by drawing it again in white, which left grey ghosts around smoothed text. Text is now drawn unsmoothed, as in the dissertation's screenshots; this is recorded in `docs/divergences.md`. I regenerated item 12's SGL snapshot for this after inspecting it.
- **Display list:** the SGL viewport added each item in a way that got quadratically slower over a run; that's fixed.
- **Stale compiled files:** my first gate run failed (39 failures in `cli-test.rkt`) because a changed module left other modules' compiled files stale. `tests/run-tests.sh` now compiles every module before testing.

The engine-side drawing code is also checked against the original in Chez by a new 50-test battery; all coordinates agree to the last bit. Of 11 deliberate code changes I made to check the new tests, 10 were caught at once. The eleventh was caught after I added one more battery case.

One thing that looks odd but I've left alone: italic digits stick out of their yellow label boxes by a pixel. The box arithmetic is the original's.

The main new files are `racket/gui/views.rkt`, `racket/gui/engine-route.rkt` and `racket/tests/workspace-view-test.rkt`. To render a moment by hand: `racket racket/tests/views-harness.rkt SCENE OUT.png`.

